+## Reefball HUD (M3-UI-01)
+
+The match HUD for the Ch7 Tidecup (SPEC §6.10; the rules are `docs/kb/design/reefball.md`). Code in `game/ui/reefball/`, layout in `game/data/ui/reefball_hud.json`, strings in `game/data/loc/reefball_hud.csv` (`RBL_HUD_*`; the engine's own names stay `RBL_*` in `strings.csv`).
+
+- **A view, not a rule.** `ReefballHud` reads a `ReefballMatch` and never writes it: the score, clock, holder, fetched state, bands and breath come from `snapshot()` and the divers; the menu is `legal_actions()` in order; each row's odds and the preview's odds, cost, end band, "scores" and who takes a miss are that option's `preview()` fields, word for word. The only engine function it calls besides is `ReefballFormulas.winded()` (the "Winded" tag and the gauge's warning line at `breath.winded_at`). Choosing only emits `action_chosen(action, target)`.
+- **`ReefballHudController`** wires one match to one HUD: on the player's contact it opens the choices and performs the one chosen; on the other side's it waits `pacing.ai_think_sec` and calls `play_ai_contact()`; after a float comes up the banner holds `pacing.goal_hold_sec`; at the end the final banner stays and `match_over(outcome, score)` goes to the flow layer (the reward hand-off is M3-C07-03's). `player_ai` lets the AI play the player's side (captures, tests); `manual` keeps waits out of `_process` (`advance()` / `flush()` drive it).
+- **Pieces** (each a HudLayout "pin", M2-UI-29): framing (match name, and the stakes from the match row's `stakes_key`, else this file's `stakes` by match id until M3-RBL-201) top left; scoreboard and clock (strokes left; in overtime, the period and "next float up wins") top; the contact line (whose contact, who holds the float and where, fetched or where to take it, and the last contact's result at its odds) under it; the opponent read (their AI profile's line from `reads`, and each opponent's band, breath and tag) top right; the drop (bands, a dot per diver, the holder ringed gold, the pass receiver ringed in focus, the miss-taker in danger, the fetch depth dashed) right; the player's side bottom right; the choices (the battle `MenuPage`, odds in the right column, sure in `heal`) bottom left with the preview beside it; the banner centre.
+- **Input parity:** ui_up / ui_down (keys and pad), hover and the wheel move the cursor and the preview follows; ui_accept or a click chooses. There is nothing to cancel on a contact. `tests/unit/test_input_parity_reefball.gd`.
+- **Layout audits:** `test_aspect_layouts.gd` `test_reefball_hud` (both capture states at 16:9, 16:10, 21:9 and 43:18, 100% and 130%), `test_pseudo_loc_screens.gd` `test_reefball_hud_fits` (both states, every option of the choice, and the final banner).
+- **Shots:** `reefball_hud_choice` (seed 7, the player's first contact, cursor on the first pass) and `reefball_hud_goal` (the AI on both sides, just after the first float comes up), drivers in `game/ui/reefball/shots/` over a plain backdrop; the arena look (`game/levels/_tests/reefball/`) is rendering's and untouched.
+- **What the engine does not tell yet** (M3-RBL-201): which opponents contest or mark an option (only who takes a miss), why an action is not legal (the menu shows legal ones only; the fetch line explains the commonest), whether a success fetches the float, and a match's stakes.
